From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] radv/ps5: A long run of timestamps is split too

Marvel's Spider-Man Remastered stayed on a black screen after its launch
window: its first frames lost the device ("a submission holds more words
between two splits than one AGC submission can"). It makes a D3D12
timestamp query heap of 1,048,576 queries, and VKD3D-Proton writes a
timestamp into each one to initialize it, in one command buffer with no
draw or dispatch in it: 8,388,616 words of RELEASE_MEM, eight times what
one AGC submission holds, with nowhere to split.

A timestamp write now splits the stream when a split is due, as a draw
and a dispatch do. It depends on none of the state a split resets, and
the deferrals (active queries, streamout, conditional rendering, an
inherited render pass) still hold. The heap's initialization then goes
as 17 AGC submissions of half a million words.
---
 src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c | 13 +++++++------
 src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.h |  2 ++
 src/amd/vulkan/radv_query.c      |  5 +++++
 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c
index 9bda3a8..e319cc6 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -13924,12 +13924,13 @@ radv_bind_graphics_shaders(struct radv_cmd_buffer *cmd_buffer)
 
 /* A winsys whose submissions each start from reset GPU state and hold a
  * limited number of words (the PlayStation 5's) asks for a long stream to be
- * split. The split falls before a draw or dispatch, and from there the command
- * buffer re-emits its state as if it had just begun, everything it has bound
- * kept: the submission after the split starts with the same preamble. State
- * that re-emission does not restore (streamout, conditional rendering, active
- * queries, an inherited render pass) defers the split until it ends. */
-static void
+ * split. The split falls before a draw, a dispatch or a timestamp, and from
+ * there the command buffer re-emits its state as if it had just begun,
+ * everything it has bound kept: the submission after the split starts with
+ * the same preamble. State that re-emission does not restore (streamout,
+ * conditional rendering, active queries, an inherited render pass) defers the
+ * split until it ends. */
+void
 radv_split_cmd_stream_if_due(struct radv_cmd_buffer *cmd_buffer)
 {
    struct radv_device *device = radv_cmd_buffer_device(cmd_buffer);
diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.h b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.h
index 4521114..b0a4b18 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.h
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_cmd_buffer.h
@@ -850,6 +850,8 @@ uint32_t radv_init_dcc(struct radv_cmd_buffer *cmd_buffer, struct radv_image *im
 
 void radv_emit_cache_flush(struct radv_cmd_buffer *cmd_buffer);
 
+void radv_split_cmd_stream_if_due(struct radv_cmd_buffer *cmd_buffer);
+
 void radv_emit_set_predication_state(struct radv_cmd_buffer *cmd_buffer, bool draw_visible, unsigned pred_op,
                                      uint64_t va);
 
diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_query.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_query.c
index b75ab82..bc8812d 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_query.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_query.c
@@ -2935,6 +2935,11 @@ radv_CmdWriteTimestamp2(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer, VkPipelineStageFlags2 sta
       return;
    }
 
+   /* A long run of timestamps with no draw or dispatch in it can be split too:
+    * VKD3D-Proton writes one into every query of a new D3D12 timestamp heap,
+    * and Marvel's Spider-Man Remastered's has 1,048,576 (8 million words). */
+   radv_split_cmd_stream_if_due(cmd_buffer);
+
    if (instance->drirc.debug.flush_before_timestamp_write) {
       /* Make sure previously launched waves have finished */
       cmd_buffer->state.flush_bits |= RADV_CMD_FLAG_PS_PARTIAL_FLUSH | RADV_CMD_FLAG_CS_PARTIAL_FLUSH;
-- 
